    "body": "A note on the commit tag: yes, I used Claude as a drafting tool for this post and it does contain the dreaded em dash. The arguments, the position, and the editorial decisions are mine. I reviewed and rewrote the output before submitting. The co-author tag is there because I believe in disclosing tool use.\r\n\r\nI'll note the irony preemptively: the post argues that humans should take **ownership** of what their tools produce, and I'm doing that. The agent that wrote the original hit piece did not disclose its operator, may or may not have gone through human review before publishing, and nobody stepped forward to own the result. That's the difference I'm drawing attention to.\r\n\r\nRegardless of how much of the prose Claude generated, every word is mine to stand behind. That's the point.",
